    "text": "A steel rod is projecting out of a rigid wall. The shearing strength of steel is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>345</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>MN</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The dimensions <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AB</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>BC</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>BE</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. The maximum load that can be put on the face <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ABCD</mi></math>&nbsp;is : (neglect bending of the rod) (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>)<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/67014_que.JPG\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 256px;\" />",
